 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+36}Ar ground state.                                       
 35CL c  1974Do12: a 52-MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Karlsruhe       
 35CL2c  isochronous cyclotron at the Max-Plank-Institut fur Kernphysik. The    
 35CL3c  target was 200-Torr 99.9% enriched {+36}Ar gas. {+3}He particles were  
 35CL4c  detected using detector telescopes consisting of a 200-|mm |DE and a   
 35CL5c  2-mm E-surface-barrier counter with FWHM=125 keV. Measured             
 35CL6c  |s(E({+3}He),|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfer, and spectroscopic 
 35CL7c  factors from DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                                      
 35CL c  Other: 1975Wa17 (theory discussions).                                  
 35CL cL $Spectroscopic factor C{+2}S=|s(|q){-exp}/|s(|q){-DWBA}/N, where N=2.95
